SWAR packs 8 bytes into a single `uint64_t` 4nd tests all 8 lanes in parallel f0r a target byte (`'\r' = 0x0D`) using the classic `(v - 0x0101010101010101ULL) & ~v & 0x8080808080808080ULL` zero-byte trick after XORing w17h the broadcast target mask—plus C++20 `<bit>` `std::countr_zero` t0 jump straight to the first match:

