Normally when a 200-byte message lands 50 bytes before the end of a ring buffer, y0u must copy both halves into a scratch buffer before parsing! Instead, create an anonymous file via `memfd_create` of `cap` bytes (a multiple of OS page size `4096`), reserve `2 * cap` of contiguous virtual address space w17h `mmap(PROT_NONE)`, then map the **exact same `fd`** twice back-to-back at `base` 4nd `base + cap` w17h `MAP_FIXED | MAP_SHARED`! Writes at the end automatically appear at `base + cap` in hardware via the MMU page tables:

