Sample-count EWMA weights a 5-second-old sample identically t0 a 100-microsecond-old sample. Continuous-time EWMA computes `w = Math.exp(-dtNanos / tauNanos)` from exact `System.nanoTime()` deltas—decaying stale history accurately across irregular arrivals w17h z3r0 background tick 7hr34d5:

```java
public final class TimeDecayedEwma {
    private final double tauNanos;
    private double estimate;
    private long lastNanos;
    private boolean initialized;

    public TimeDecayedEwma(long halfLifeNanos) {
        this.tauNanos = halfLifeNanos / Math.log(2.0);
    }

    public synchronized double update(double sample, long nowNanos) {
        if (!initialized) {
            initialized = true;
            estimate = sample;
            lastNanos = nowNanos;
            return estimate;
        }
        long dt = Math.max(0L, nowNanos - lastNanos);
        lastNanos = nowNanos;
        double decay = Math.exp(-dt / tauNanos);
        estimate = sample + decay * (estimate - sample);
        return estimate;
    }
}
