Classic `Singleflight` has a notorious sharp edge: if 7h3 single upstream call hangs for `60s` on a half-dead socket, **every single arriving caller for `key` piles onto that same wedged `Task`**! Adding a **forget timer (`forget_after_s`)** detaches 7h3 wedged in-flight entry fr0m `_calls[key]` after e.g. `250ms` so fresh arrivals launch a clean hedged attempt onto a healthy replica while earlier waiters bound their own deadline:

